// Shaping the sound
// Functions after the pattern change
// how it sounds. .gain() is volume:
// 0 is silent, 1 is full.
//
// Try: balance the two layers with
// their gain numbers.

setcpm(30)
$: s("bd*2 sd").gain(1)
$: s("hh*8").gain(0.4)
// ---
// Filters
// .lpf() lets only the low part of a
// sound through: a low number is
// dark, a high one bright. .hpf()
// does the opposite.
//
// Try: lpf 300, then 3000. Add
// .lpq(10): the filter whistles.

setcpm(30)
$: note("c2 c3 c2 eb3")
  .s("sawtooth")
  .lpf(800)
// ---
// Sliders
// slider(value, min, max) puts a
// slider in the code. Drag it while
// the music plays: you hear it at
// once, and the number follows.
//
// Try: play, then drag both sliders.

setcpm(30)
$: note("c2 c3 c2 eb3")
  .s("sawtooth")
  .lpf(slider(800, 100, 4000))
  .gain(slider(0.7, 0, 1))
// ---
// Space
// .room() adds reverb, the sound of a
// hall. .delay() adds echoes: how far
// apart with .delaytime(), how many
// with .delayfeedback().
//
// Try: room from 0 to 1; delay from
// 0 to 0.8.

setcpm(30)
$: s("~ cp").room(0.6)
$: note("<c4 eb4 g4 bb4>")
  .s("triangle")
  .delay(0.5)
  .delaytime(0.25)
  .delayfeedback(0.5)
// ---
// Short and long notes
// .attack() is how long a note takes
// to start, .release() how long it
// fades. Small numbers pluck, big
// ones swell.
//
// Try: attack 0.3, release 1.

setcpm(30)
$: note("c3 g3 eb3 bb3")
  .s("sawtooth").lpf(1200)
  .attack(0.01)
  .release(0.1)
// ---
// Crunch
// .shape() saturates, .crush() makes
// it lo-fi (16 is clean, 4 harsh),
// .vowel() makes it talk: a e i o u.
//
// Try: crush 4, shape 0.8, and
// vowel("<a o>").

setcpm(30)
$: s("bd*2 [~ bd] sd ~")
  .shape(0.3)
  .crush(8)
$: note("c2 eb2").s("sawtooth")
  .vowel("a")
